{
 "_readme": [
  "Author names as the Patrologia bio file spells them, mapped to the name",
  "the catalogue uses. Both name the same person; one is the Latin form and",
  "the other is the English. Without this the life is never found and the",
  "page says no biography has been written, which is false.",
  "",
  "Generated 2026-09-11 and reviewed by hand. The rule that produced it:",
  "the PERSONAL name must match (first name part, allowing a one-letter",
  "ending difference for Latin case), AND at least one further part must",
  "match. A looser rule that allowed any shared token proposed",
  "'Peter Abaelardus' -> 'Peter Ram' and 'Dunstanus of Canterbury' ->",
  "'Odo of Canterbury', matching the PLACE rather than the person. Putting",
  "the wrong life on an author is worse than putting none, so the loose",
  "rule was thrown away rather than filtered.",
  "",
  "151 of the 233 orphaned entries are still unmatched and still invisible.",
  "They need a person to look at them, not a better regex."
 ],
